\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Hard-split mechanism and query difficulty profile. The hard stream keeps only a minority of target simulator-state observations as direct evidence, while downgrading or dropping the rest. The resulting workload emphasizes temporal and provenance queries and produces graded known, unknown, uncertain, and conflicting answer conditions across target predicates.}}{11}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:hard-profile}{{2}{11}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Aggregated long state-chain templates. The 30-episode long subset adds multi-stage temporal maintenance cases, such as actuator, temperature, hot, cooked, and frozen state chains, to the larger short-transition benchmark.}}{11}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:long-chain}{{3}{11}}
